sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-levin-youtube-channel-math-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "@drmichaellevin 8-law mathematical synthesis & biological-law-criteria suite — MorphoEval overall 57.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-24"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3.1 referee score of the pruned 8-law `@drmichaellevin` synthesis suite: 57.4/100 (this file's first issue 44.8 on the Pass 3 tree; v2 26.4 on the 25-law version; v1 self-score 93.8), verdict band 'partially faithful', 2.6 points below 'mostly faithful'. Eight of the ten Pass 3 remediation items are closed on the evidence: Law 1 is now scored and asserted on its BVP reach (32.01 cells, 1.0 at G_gj = 0) and plotted; Law 4's breakdown is real (fixed exit rates, non-doubly-stochastic routing: slope -1.0000 -> +0.1866); Law 3 is a central-difference discretisation with measured O(h^2) convergence to the Boltzmann ratio; Law 6 runs a 3-node conditioning ODE (0.0015 -> 1.0) and labels Delta E = -eta N^2 an identity; assertions are parameterised and precede the writes; 13/14 CLI flags work; both input hashes are pinned and asserted; the catalog taxonomy, README hash, KG payload, math-KG loci, C4/C2 tags and verify_integrity.py are fixed. Two are not: the Ross DOI is wrong a second time (10.1017/9781009301435 does not resolve; the Element is 10.1017/9781009300940, 2025) and `froese2024` still has a paraphrased title and a co-author Crossref does not list; and nothing is committed. New in Pass 3.1: the documentation reports numbers the code does not produce (criteria doc \"+0.7618\" for the Law 4 breakdown and \"0.0020 -> 0.9036\" for Law 6, repeated in the math-KG YAML and KG payload; Law 6's docstring lists a different ODE and different results from the code; the header promises 101 G_gj values, a Hill fit with RMS residual, alpha to 0.95 and GRN weight plasticity / extinction that are not implemented). The module remains a synthesis/aggregator with no specimen of its own and no comparison with any published measurement, which caps specimen-match and morphometric-validation. Overall 57.4/100 (faithfulness 49.4, reproducibility 75.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 1969a7ea; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, lean 4.35.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 72, Morphological realism / specimen match 24, Parameter expressivity 76, Morphometric validation 44, Source and data traceability 74, Code-to-model traceability 78, Reproducibility package 76. Output judged: media/levin_youtube_channel_math_synthesis.png: rendered output of models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py, not present when the audit was snapshotted (unfingerprinted). Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cf60fdd1887c234204e281c3b23afa4f191e046d38cdfdc9431520113f92b430; artifact_sha256: 1b921945d2f665bce01dcd2bd4394572807c93e6d3b702050fdbc7b31a75e03f; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/levin_youtube_channel/levin_youtube_catalog.json=216a474f76c137c3..., datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib=3f0fc6ec4051750b..., sorting-morphogenesis/figures/quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json=b54103b87a1f5d77...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-24-levin-youtube-channel-math-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Cervera, Levin & Mafe (2020): voltage-gated gap-junction coupling G_ij(V_i, V_j) = G_0 / [(1 + e^{(V_i - V_th)/V_0})(1 + e^{(V_j - V_th)/V_0})] with polarising and depolarising channel currents; depolarised domains electrically isolate | Pietak & Levin (2016, 2017): Nernst-Planck electrodiffusion in BETSE; at zero flux the charged-morphogen ratio is Boltzmann, exp(-zF dV / RT), independent of gap-junction permeability | Chvykov et al. (2021): low-rattling principle P_ss ∝ exp(-gamma R) tested on smarticle collectives and simulation; the 'rattling' is a diffusion-tensor quantity, not a scalar exit rate | Watson & Szathmary (2016): natural induction / Hebbian deepening of visited attractors; Pigozzi, Goldstein & Levin (2025): associative conditioning in continuous GRN ODE models with measured conditioning success; Biswas et al. (2023): pathway-level memory in transcriptional network models | Hoel et al. (2013), Hoel (2026): causal emergence via effective information and the determinism/degeneracy decomposition CP = det - deg | Levin (2019, 2022): TAME cognitive light cone (diagrammatic); Bongard & Levin (2023): polycomputing (conceptual); Shreesha & Levin (2025): agent-based spatial Prisoner's Dilemma with controllable borders; reconstructed_in_script: Law 1 (L177-L225): N-cell linear diffusion-leak BVP -G (V_{i-1} - 2V_i + V_{i+1}) + (G_half/N) V_i = delta_{i0}; reach L = sum_i V_i / V_0 at G_gj in {0, 0.5, 1.0} and on a 51-point grid; continuum sqrt(1/k) tanh(N sqrt(k)); Hill curve 1 + (N-1) G/(G + G_half) computed but unused | Law 2 (L231-L277, unchanged since Pass 3): 20-cell ODE, cells 0-4 clamped at -10 mV, cubic bistable I_ion with roots -60 / -38 / -10 mV (not Cervera's channel currents), Bell-Boltzmann vs ohmic G_ij, RK45 to t = 80 | Law 3 (L283-L331): 1-D zero-flux BVP with central-difference / Pade(1,1) edge coefficients a_i = G(-1 + dv/2), b_{i+1} = G(1 + dv/2) on a linear voltage profile; grid refinement N_ap = 15..240 and a 5-value G_gj sweep at N_ap = 120 | Law 4 (L337-L404): 24-state CTMC, W(i->j) = r_i^gamma K_ij(alpha) with K(alpha) = (1 - alpha) K_sym + alpha K_trap, K_sym Sinkhorn-symmetrised doubly stochastic, K_trap row-normalised weights linspace(0.1, 2.5)^2.5 (column sums != 1); stationary vector from L^T p = 0; log-log fit of p against the fixed r_exit at alpha = 0, 0.5, 0.9 | Laws 5 and 7 (L410-L449): 4-row x 3-gate truth table; S_6 CE2 numbers read from the hash-pinned sorting-morphogenesis JSON | Law 6 (L455-L540): 16-gene symmetric J, Hebbian J += eta s s^T for 15 epochs, energy trace, basin fraction over 120 four-flip trials; 3-node ODE dx_CS = -x_CS + I_CS, dx_M = -0.02 x_M + 0.25 sigma(12 (x_CS x_US - 0.5)), dx_US = -x_US + sigma(12 (I_US + 0.9 x_M x_CS - 0.55)) in four phases (CS test, paired training t = 25, washout t = 5, CS test t = 10) | Law 8 (L546-L580, unchanged): pi_C(k) = (1 - k^-1/2) b - c and pi_D(k) = b k^-1/2 over k = 1..36; exact m x m directed bond count for m = 1..6 | 8 Lean theorems (Loop L30-L288, unchanged since Pass 3; duplicated in MathOfBiology.lean L1200-L1375), each on Nat/Int/Bool reductions of the law; transfer_boundary: The 8 laws are evaluated on synthetic parameter sets chosen by the builder (cubic current coefficients, r_exit table, K_trap weights, J ~ N(0, 0.25), 3-node ODE gains, b = 2, c = 1); no quantity is compared with a value measured in Cervera 2020, Pietak 2016/2017, Chvykov 2021, Pigozzi 2025 or Shreesha 2025 | Law 4's breakdown is now a genuine property of the model (non-doubly-stochastic routing with fixed exit rates), but K_trap is a builder construction and the magnitude of the breakdown is misreported in the criteria doc (+0.7618 vs the computed +0.1866) | Law 3's grid-refinement convergence is a genuine numerical check of the discretisation against the Boltzmann closed form; the G_gj invariance is still linear algebra (G_gj scales Q) | Law 1's BVP and its continuum closed form agree to 1.6 %; the Hill formula the law was previously scored on disagrees with the BVP by RMS 55 cells over the grid and is now neither the metric nor fitted, despite the docstring | Law 6's 3-node ODE is a hand-tuned minimal conditioning circuit, not a model from Pigozzi 2025 or Biswas 2023, and its docstring describes a different circuit with different results | Law 8's k >= 17 strict-dominance threshold applies 1 - 1/sqrt(k) to non-square k that no m x m cluster realises; the first exact square with strict dominance is k = 25; does_not_claim: This audit does not claim any of the 8 source equations is wrong as published, nor that any Lean theorem fails to check (all 8 compile with 0 sorry); it scores whether the suite implements, exercises and validates the laws and whether the O1/O2, T1-T4 and C1-C6 tags are earned by linked artefacts | It does not verify the content of the 63 cited videos (no transcripts offline) and does not recompute the S_6 TPM behind quantifying_emergence_ce2_metrics.json; it re-checks only the arithmetic consistency of the imported numbers | It does not score the 17 CHANNEL_CONCEPTS_INDEX items, which are correctly excluded from law status." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Commit the whole Pass 3.1 package (script, Loop .lean, YAML, docs, bib, README, catalog, KG payload, summary JSON, verify_integrity.py) so a checkpoint commit exists, and re-run this audit against that commit. Then the remaining ceiling is structural: wire at least one law to a published measurement (Chvykov 2021 Fig. 2-3 enrichment, Pigozzi 2025 conditioning success, Cervera 2020 voltage levels or Pietak 2016 BETSE gradients) so specimen-match and morphometric-validation can move.",
            "remediation needed: Make the written record match the code, then re-run: docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md L62 (+0.7618 -> +0.1866 or whatever the pinned run gives), L64 and morphoeval/math_kg_loops/levin-youtube-channel-math.yaml L112 and docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json L583 (0.0020 -> 0.9036 -> 0.0015 -> 1.0); script header L12 (101 -> 51), L25 (0.95 -> 0.90), L33-L35 (remove 'weight plasticity' and 'extinction' or implement them); Law 6 docstring L461-L469 (write the ODE that is in L506-L514 with its actual results). Generate these numbers from the summary JSON rather than typing them.",
            "remediation needed: datasets/levin_youtube_channel/paper_citations.bib:154-164 - set froese2024's title to 'Irruption and Absorption: A Black-Box Framework for How Mind and Matter Make a Difference to Each Other' and its author list to the Crossref record (Froese T), or document the source of the additional author; drop the 'Causal emergence 2.0:' prefix from hoel2026ce2 or note that it is not in the Crossref title. Add identifiers (or remove the names) for Stoica, Morozov, Albantakis (2024) and Sweet (2026).",
            "remediation needed: docs/BIOLOGICAL_LAW_CRITERIA.md:31 - replace 10.1017/9781009301435 with 10.1017/9781009300940 (Ross LN, Explanation in Biology, Cambridge University Press, 2025) and the year 2024 with 2025; verify by GET on api.crossref.org/works/<doi> before committing, as the V5 rule requires.",
            "remediation needed: docs/bioelectricity/levin_youtube_kg.json - remove or regenerate `verified_measurements` (currently the referee's Pass 3 sidecar describing superseded code) and reconcile L583 with L1150; commit the script that generates the payload and the script that regenerates the catalog's mappedMathLaws so both artefacts are rebuildable.",
            "remediation needed: models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py:177-225 (Law 1) - either implement what L182-L183 promise (fit G_eff of the Hill form to pde_reach_curve, report the RMS residual, assert it) or delete the Hill sentences and the dead `hill_curve`. Give Law 1 its own panel or a proper secondary x-axis with G_gj ticks instead of g_grid * 9.5 on the cell-index axis (L608).",
            "remediation needed: models/2026-levin-channel-math-synthesis.py:823-825 - make `--law` skip the solvers and panels it excludes; relax L841 to a non-strict test (or skip it) when delta_v_mv = 0; record the git commit, timestamp and script SHA-256 in the summary JSON." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.574"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (Anthropic; independent cross-provider MorphoEval referee, Pass 3 / 3.1)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

